# daikintomqtt — project brief

Bridge between Daikin Onecta Cloud API and MQTT (Jeedom / Home Assistant).

**Read first:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and [docs/architecture.md](../../docs/architecture.md).

## Stack

Node >= 20, TypeScript strict, CommonJS, `src/` → `dist/`. Entry: `daikinToMQTT.js` → `dist/main.js`.

## Commands

```bash
npm run build          # Required before apiCoverageAudit test
npm start              # Production
npm run run            # Dev (ts-node)
node test/unit/apiCoverageAudit.test.js   # After build
```

## Conventions

- Tabs, global `logger` with `[file.ts] => msg` format
- Property keys prefixed `_` (e.g. `_onOffMode`)
- Enums: `typeEnum`, `converterEnum` from `typeConstants.ts`
- Commits: Conventional Commits; changelog EN + FR

## Don'ts

- Do not modify `daikinRCCloud` for new mappings (auto via MQTT)
- Do not edit `src/daikin-cloud/**` unless fixing cloud client
- Do not bypass `enqueueWriteForDevice` or add ad-hoc API polling
- Do not commit `config/settings.yml` or tokens

